WEBVTT

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.490
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.660
The Café Yard!

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:37.350
Miss Sasako,

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:41.910
I'm in the mood today to 
be praised by others.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:43.560
I see.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.470
Then I will quickly praise you.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.330
Miss Sasako,

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:51.270
don't you have a little more 
time to kindly talk with me...

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:55.380
You know, never mind. 
Please go back to work.

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:58.120
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:01:58.120 --> 00:01:59.730
What is it, Panda?

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:01.400
Sorry.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.900
I don't feel like praising you.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:07.720
You're going to give up 
right from the start.

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:11.900
That's okay. I'll call my mom later.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.760
Miss Sasako,

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:17.430
I got some good broccoli and 
mushrooms from the garden,

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:20.000
so let's make today's 
lunch special pasta.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:20.860
Sure.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:24.700
Wow, they look so fresh and delicious.

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:28.260
Hey, Polar Bear,

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:31.290
I've always wondered...

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:35.020
What? Your future plans?

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:37.820
I wonder about that, too, 
but that's not it.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:39.770
Then what is it?

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:43.260
Do you always get vegetables 
from the vegetable garden out there?

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.040
Yep. From the Café's 
vegetable garden.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.390
Didn't I tell you?

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.340
Nope. First time I heard about it.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:53.020
Well that's because I didn't 
tell you, Mr. Penguin.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.320
I wonder if I'm the 
only one you didn't tell.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:56.400
Oh well, whatever.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:00.900
By the way, what does the 
Café's yard look like?

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.020
Sounds like it's pretty big.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:07.410
I live right next door, 
but I have no idea.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:12.120
Daily Lunch Special Menu

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:12.120
Come to think of it, there are things
 I don't know about it, either.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:14.050
Do you want to go see?

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:15.680
Definitely!

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.590
Me, too! Me, too!

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:20.050
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.790
Shall we go, then?

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:24.470
Yeah.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.440
Let's.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:26.100
Yes.

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:29.380
Oh?

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:30.970
You, too, Miss Sasako?

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:34.240
Oh, yes. I'd like to go, too.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:37.260
But then there'd be no one 
to watch the café.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.450
That's true...

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:43.750
Hello.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.740
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:51.580
First, we have the open terrace.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.460
Let's skip this.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.100
We know this part.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:56.410
Mr. Penguin.

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:57.170
What?

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.760
That's my house over there.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:02.200
Huh?

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.980
Maybe it's over here?

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:07.790
Hey, do you know where it is?

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:10.600
You can be quiet now.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.610
I guess it doesn't hurt to ask.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.610
Mr. Llama is such a nice guy.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:25.490
Welcome.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:27.950
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:33.160
That's Mr. Tree Kangaroo's 
Coffee Roasting Plant.

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:36.330
Oh hi, Mr. Polar Bear.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.470
Thanks for your hard work.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.100
We already know this place, 
so we're skipping it.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.380
What?! You're leaving already?

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:46.240
Let's take our time looking around.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:47.700
But if we take too long,

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.450
we might not be able to 
see everything in one day.

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:53.480
I had no idea this yard was so big.

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:56.270
Well, we'll see.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:59.120
Guess you'll just have 
to see for yourself.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:01.550
Such a tease.

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:06.280
What kind of tree is this?

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:08.010
It's a cherry tree.

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:10.420
We did our cherry blossom viewing here last spring.

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:13.080
Oh, I remember that.

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:20.900
This is the first time I've seen a 
cherry blossom tree in the fall,

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:22.830
but it's quite nice this 
time of the year, too.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:25.800
I don't remember that day much.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:29.680
That's because you always 
drink so much, Mr. Penguin.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.810
You look just like Mr. Nagura!

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:36.320
Oh, mushrooms!

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:37.870
Those are Brick Cap mushrooms.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:38.780
They're edible.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:41.110
Ow!

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:43.960
Oh, there might be some 
chestnuts on the ground.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:45.110
Say something sooner!

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:48.000
This is the first time I've seen

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.560
an Akebia tree bear fruit.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:52.120
You eat them when
 they look ready to burst.

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:57.010
There's so much, even though 
we haven't walked that far.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.580
Hey, what's that?

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:05.510
Oh, that's...

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.930
Sloth

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:14.820
I guess Sloth did have a house.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:19.400
But it doesn't look like 
he's home much.

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:22.900
Why does he even get the paper?

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:28.560
I wonder if he's out right now.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:35.240
Over there, is the vegetable garden.

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:37.270
Over here...

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:38.460
What's over there?

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:42.050
You wanna know?

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:44.990
I have a bad feeling about 
this, so never mind.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:46.630
If you go that way...

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:49.170
Never mind! Let's go to the next place!

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:58.720
So this is where the 
vegetable garden is.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:01.470
Hello.

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:03.650
What brings you all out here today?

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:07.520
This is the kangaroos' 
vegetable garden.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:08.710
Thanks for having us.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:12.510
The food served at 
Polar Bear's Café

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:15.820
is made with fresh garden vegetables.

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:18.370
That's why it's so delicious.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:21.910
There's also an orchard 
right over there.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:26.550
Juice made from freshly 
picked fruit is the best.

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:30.140
Oh, I see...

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:32.650
Could you stop for a bit?

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:34.010
I feel nauseous.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:36.850
Oh, you can stop.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:39.190
So, what brings you here today?

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.230
Are you here to help us out?

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:45.440
Well, no. Today, all of us ar—

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:48.090
Huh?

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:51.870
Are we really doing this again?

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.580
Hey!

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:59.130
Why'd you go on without me?

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:00.610
Sorry about that.

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:02.590
Our legs moved on their own.

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:04.880
The heck is up with that lame excuse?

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:09.630
You're not going to help 
the kangaroos out?

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:11.090
I'll help out later.

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:12.630
After we've seen the whole yard.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:15.260
I'll go, too. And this is...

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:18.290
Prairie Dog's herb garden.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:23.390
So you even grow all the 
herbs in the yard, too.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:27.380
Ooh, what's that?

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:29.560
Miss Sasako is excited.

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:31.490
Oh, that's...

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:34.200
Cheese Workshop

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:41.440
The lemurs' mozzarella 
cheese workshop.

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:43.470
Wow.

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:45.770
So the cheese is homemade, too.

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:46.910
Didn't I tell you?

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:50.090
Nope. In general, 
you don't tell me anything.

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:53.560
So monkeys were making it.

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:57.120
They're quite the artisans.

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:01.290
Huh?

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:03.400
What are those?

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:05.230
Water buffaloes.

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:09.950
Our mozzarella cheese is 
authentic and is made

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:14.950
from water buffalo milk 
rather than regular milk.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:20.830
Mozzarella cheese made from fresh 
 water buffalo milk is the best.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:27.920
I want to have a taste 
without helping out at all.

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:31.690
You're brutally honest, aren't you?

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:33.960
Here you go.

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:38.010
Wow, it's so light and fluffy!

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:43.620
It's so rich and delicious.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:46.020
Let's make pizza with 
this cheese later.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:48.480
Okay, let's go back now!

00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:51.130
I'm not going to help at all,

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:53.300
but let's hurry and eat pizza.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:56.540
We know you're brutally 
honest, but could you

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:58.490
wait until we're done looking?

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.560
I can't believe this is your yard.

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:06.210
It's huge.

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:07.350
Come on.

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:10.100
Let's hurry and go back 
so we can eat pizza.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:12.670
You really don't hold back, do you?

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:17.440
Huh? A hammock in a place like this?

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:20.200
Yes. I take naps here sometimes.

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:23.270
Wow, that sounds great.

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:29.750
Could you give me a lift, Polar Bear?

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:30.350
Sure.

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:33.570
Oh, sorry.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:34.920
That hurt.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:37.420
Apparently I got to experience 
the worst before the best.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.740
This is great.

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:45.690
Mr. Penguin, let me try already.

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:50.130
What do you mean, "already"? 
I just got up here.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:54.260
Now, now. Don't be like that.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:57.670
Let's all get in.

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:59.590
There's no room.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:02.160
By the way...

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:04.450
I wonder if Mr. Llama 
is doing all right.

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:06.660
He said he'd be all right,

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:08.060
so I'm sure he's all right.

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:14.730
Thanks for waiting. 
Here's your caffè latte and cappuccino.

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:17.740
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:23.240
And this is where I practice golfing.

00:11:23.840 --> 00:11:27.060
Must be nice. Can I come next time?

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:29.660
Of course. And then over there...

00:11:30.380 --> 00:11:33.300
I play basketball with 
Grizzly sometimes.

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:40.070
Up ahead is an obstacle course.

00:11:40.070 --> 00:11:42.660
And over there is a 
small fishing pond.

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:47.440
Your days must be really 
fun, Polar Bear,

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:48.890
even though you're a café owner.

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:52.310
Maybe I'll work here, too.

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:54.310
You fail.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:56.880
Oh, thank goodness.

00:11:56.880 --> 00:12:00.210
I was wondering what I'd 
do if I actually passed.

00:12:00.770 --> 00:12:05.320
I get the feeling you go through 
every day purely on impulse.

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:08.590
And what's down this way?

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:12.280
It's better that you don't go.

00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:13.250
Why is that?

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:16.460
Do you want to know?

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:18.390
No, never mind.

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:33.430
The yard here really is huge.

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:37.650
I wonder what's in that area 
where we weren't supposed to go.

00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:41.150
Thanks for your hard work, Mr. Llama.

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:42.680
Order whatever you'd like.

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:44.320
Oh, don't worry about me.

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:46.730
Here you go, pizza.

00:12:48.380 --> 00:12:49.170
Huh?

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:57.370
Seems you really wanted 
that pizza, Polar Bear.

00:12:57.370 --> 00:12:59.840
He was walking rather 
briskly on the way back.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:03.050
Thank you for the food!

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:10.970
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:15.890
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:14.980
Sales Penguins' Sales!

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:20.400
And now, let us begin our 
monthly business meeting.

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:24.820
The first subject at hand is the 
sales of the penguin cards.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:27.760
The results of Adélie penguin's idea

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:31.130
of promoting the cards 
as a game of Memory

00:13:31.130 --> 00:13:34.900
is an unbelievable 180% rise 
in sales just this past month,

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:36.970
even in these hard times.

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:42.570
Well done, Adélie, with your 
charismatic sales approach.

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:43.930
Oh, stop it.

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:46.220
It was all because of your leadership.

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:47.250
No, no.

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:48.930
We can thank Chinstrap for

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:51.090
bringing it all in when we needed to.

00:13:51.090 --> 00:13:53.060
It's because of all our hard work.

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:55.690
You're right!

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:57.220
It was all of us!

00:13:58.210 --> 00:13:59.810
Thank you for waiting.

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:06.490
Um, you sell two decks 
in a set, right?

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:10.200
Yes, because they're used to play Memory.

00:14:10.940 --> 00:14:12.130
But doesn't that mean that

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:14.410
fewer people purchased them?

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:21.420
Could you not butt in
suddenly like that?!

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:24.340
My apologies. Please enjoy.

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:29.590
I guess people don't care 
about penguins after all.

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:32.240
Let's not say that.

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:36.030
I wonder if there's a place 
where penguin lovers gather.

00:14:36.030 --> 00:14:37.540
Of course there isn't.

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:39.600
Don't give up so easily!

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:43.100
Welcome.

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:44.420
Thanks for your hard work.

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:45.910
Are you done with work for the day?

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:49.030
You're so mean, Polar Bear.

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:54.600
Why won't you make 
deliveries to the zoo?

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:55.910
Oh, that's because...

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:58.410
It's troublesome.

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:01.420
That's true. I totally understand.

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:05.940
You two somehow seem to have the most

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:07.380
pleasantly straightforward conversations.

00:15:07.870 --> 00:15:10.040
Oh! I just got an idea!

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:11.340
What? What?

00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:13.650
The zoo!

00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:15.760
Let's have the zoo sell our cards!

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:21.230
Penguin

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:18.700
They get lots of animal lovers,

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:21.230
so I'm sure they'll happily buy them.

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:24.270
I wonder if they'd let us 
sell them there though.

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:28.030
So we just have to pitch the idea

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:30.580
that by selling the cards there,

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:32.850
the zoo would get more visitors, too.

00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:34.330
I see.

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:38.700
So they get more customers 
and we sell more cards.

00:15:39.010 --> 00:15:40.120
All right.

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:43.170
Let's take this idea 
home and think on it.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:44.950
See ya.

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:46.330
Hey, wait a sec!

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:47.880
Why are you going home?!

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:49.820
Huh? We're not going to think on it?

00:15:49.820 --> 00:15:50.650
We are!

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:51.850
But right here, right now!

00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:57.740
We originally made these 
cards because there are

00:15:57.740 --> 00:16:00.180
a lot of different kinds 
of penguins, right?

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:02.160
Yep.

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:07.010
So we just need an idea for how to appeal 
even more to the characteristics of penguins.

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:08.240
I see, I see.

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:11.150
Something so all sorts of 
penguins can get in on the action.

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:14.000
Like some penguin action hero show?

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:17.080
That's it!

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:18.620
That's a great idea!

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:20.750
I'll be the lead!

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:23.410
Adélienger!

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:25.750
Hey, no fair! Then I'm gonna be...

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:28.960
Gentooman.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:30.760
But you're not a man.

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:35.240
I'm... Chinstrapger!

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:38.140
Sounds sort of like a villain.

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:41.350
I think your face is a 
little dull to be a hero.

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:42.710
What?!

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:45.890
Putting that aside, 
since we're talking action heroes,

00:16:45.890 --> 00:16:48.150
how about we all be heroes?

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:49.650
You're right!

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:52.500
We'll be the heroes!

00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:56.570
And be super popular with the kids.

00:16:57.350 --> 00:16:59.830
And the penguin cards 
will be a smash hit.

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:04.600
This sounds like it might just work!

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:07.420
All right, let's ready 
our presentation.

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:08.540
Roger!

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:11.490
They seem really excited 
about something.

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:12.720
Yeah!

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:15.200
Let's hurry and get started!

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:17.470
So, Mr. Penguin, 
you're just going to keep living

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:19.330
your boring, mundane life,

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:22.350
without getting excited 
about anything, right?

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:26.010
Hey! I get excited sometimes, too!

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:28.170
Like when I eat delicious sashimi!

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:31.190
Forget it. I'll just shut up now.

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:38.240
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:45.860
Thank you very much 
for your time today.

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:48.800
Here is my business card.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:49.130
Penguin Card Sales Promotion Team
Sales Associate
Adélie penguin
Genus Pygoscelis

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:54.360
Mr. Adélie penguin,  
of the Genus Pygoscelis,

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:55.760
sales associate of the

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:58.590
Penguin Card Sales Promotion Team?

00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:03.130
And I would be the team 
director, Gentoo penguin.

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:05.770
And I am Chinstrap penguin, 
in charge of accounting.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:09.060
My name is Handa. 
I'm a zookeeper here.

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:10.830
Please, have a seat.

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:12.590
We're already seated.

00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:13.340
Oh, right.

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:15.990
You look like you're standing
even when you're sitting.

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:17.930
My apologies.

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:20.990
What can I do for you today?

00:18:21.350 --> 00:18:22.560
Right.

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:27.460
We are trying to promote 
these penguin cards.

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:32.280
We created them so people could learn 
 the various kinds of penguins, but...

00:18:33.890 --> 00:18:36.900
We were hoping that you might consider

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:38.830
selling them in your shop.

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:39.590
Yes!

00:18:40.230 --> 00:18:42.170
Penguin cards?

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:45.560
We have had similar offers...

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:49.580
However, our space is limited

00:18:49.580 --> 00:18:50.600
so adding items...

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:52.260
Of course!

00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:54.220
Of course!

00:18:54.220 --> 00:18:58.640
Not only are we trying 
to sell these cards,

00:18:58.640 --> 00:19:01.250
but we'd like to present to you an idea

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:04.700
on how to increase 
your visitor numbers.

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:05.630
Huh?

00:19:05.630 --> 00:19:08.080
We'll let this speak for itself.

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:12.230
Has your zoo...

00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:16.420
...fallen into a rut?

00:19:18.410 --> 00:19:22.390
Bring an innovative new 
attraction to your zoo.

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:27.140
Penguin Action Hero Show!

00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:30.640
Penguin Action Hero Show?

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:32.710
Wh-What the—

00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:37.600
At the end of the 21st century...

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:39.260
A peculiar event was occurring at

00:19:39.260 --> 00:19:41.850
the South Pole due to global warming.

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:50.130
From now on the islands 
of the South Pole

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:52.880
will be ruled by the Genus Eudyptes!

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:56.160
Help!

00:20:01.520 --> 00:20:02.530
Oh no!

00:20:02.530 --> 00:20:04.280
The little one is going to 
be attacked by the bad guys!

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:05.600
Hold it right there!

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:09.060
You'll have to face us!

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:11.070
Who goes there?!

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:15.190
Gentooger!

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:19.820
Chinstrapger!

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:23.740
Adélienger!

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:32.480
South Pole Squad

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:35.040
Penguinger!

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:39.510
How... cool!

00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:43.370
And this would be where 
the battle starts.

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:44.190
Where's the rest?

00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:47.720
The Penguingers fight to defeat 
the forces of evil

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:51.230
until peace is restored 
to the South Pole.

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:52.630
How does that sound?

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:54.720
That's great!

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:57.770
I always loved action hero shows as a kid!

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:58.460
Right?!

00:20:58.460 --> 00:20:59.890
Thank you for all your hard work.

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:01.400
Thanks!

00:21:02.180 --> 00:21:07.150
How about we sell these cards 
to go along with this show?

00:21:07.150 --> 00:21:09.360
That's a great idea!

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:10.660
I'd love to see the rest!

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:12.870
I'll immediately bring it 
up at the project meeting.

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:15.580
All right!

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:17.970
Penguingers!

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:19.090
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:27.160
Wow, so the zoo is doing a 
penguin action hero show now?

00:21:27.570 --> 00:21:28.840
Yep.

00:21:28.840 --> 00:21:31.310
Mr. Handa's really excited.

00:21:33.760 --> 00:21:35.810
It seems really fun.

00:21:36.660 --> 00:21:39.180
Maybe I'll make panda cards

00:21:39.180 --> 00:21:42.280
and do a panda action hero 
show with the others.

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:44.130
Pandaman!

00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:48.450
Do you have even a shred of integrity?

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:49.660
What?

00:21:50.210 --> 00:21:52.890
It'd be a big hit.

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:57.250
It'd be a total rip off.

00:21:58.100 --> 00:22:01.010
How about North Pole 
Cop: Polar Bearian?

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:03.210
Sea Anemone!

00:22:03.850 --> 00:22:08.880
And now, let's see that 0.05 
second process one more time.

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:10.930
That's a rip off, too.

00:22:11.620 --> 00:22:14.220
How about we change gears

00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:16.560
and I do some traditional 
comedic story telling?

00:22:20.620 --> 00:22:21.900
That's rather dull.

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:24.480
Yes, very dull.

00:23:54.910 --> 00:24:25.010
Next Time

00:23:58.350 --> 00:23:59.710
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.710 --> 00:24:00.870
What is it, Panda?

00:24:00.870 --> 00:24:03.170
Could you possibly be the link

00:24:03.170 --> 00:24:05.570
to me somehow getting 
royalties from hit songs?

00:24:05.570 --> 00:24:07.480
I think that'd be rather difficult.

00:24:07.480 --> 00:24:10.250
You give up so easily, Mr. Penguin.

00:24:10.250 --> 00:24:11.590
I think it depends on the situation.

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:15.380
Then I'll give you three seconds 
to do whatever you'd like.

00:24:15.380 --> 00:24:16.550
That's rather short.

00:24:16.550 --> 00:24:17.890
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:17.890 --> 00:24:19.430
Next week's Polar Bear's Café

00:24:19.430 --> 00:24:21.100
will be broadcast in analog.

00:24:21.100 --> 00:24:22.810
It will be broadcast in digital.

00:24:21.730 --> 00:24:24.550
Panda Corner Contest
Coffee Roaster Masaki
Panda Corner Project

00:24:22.810 --> 00:24:24.110
Enjoy!
